All four findings fixed, all four gates re-run green.

**1. BLOCKER — vacuous escape test** (`src/repl/editor.rs`)
`PlainSource::read_line` paints its prompt, so a pipe under `REDBLUE_COLOR=always` *does* emit escapes and the old test (`!source.highlights()`) could not fail. Split `painted_prompt` out of `read_line` so the bytes are testable, renamed the test to `edge_a_piped_session_paints_its_prompt_and_never_its_input`, and asserted the actual output: no highlighter on the pipe path, byte-identical prompt with colour off, exactly `paint(Prompt, ..)` — two escapes, one open one close — with colour on. Corrected the two doc comments that claimed pipes can emit no escape at all. Pinned end-to-end too: `tests/repl_test.rs::edge_a_piped_session_prompts_plainly_until_colour_is_asked_for` runs the real binary with the colour vars cleared (no escape in the output) and with `REDBLUE_COLOR=always` (painted prompt), via a new `session_with_env` that sets vars on the child only.

**2. MAJOR — `!!` over `:prompt rb> ` lost the space** (`mod.rs`, `commands.rs`)
`session_loop` recorded `trim()` while dispatching `trim_start()`. Now records a line the way it is dispatched, for commands whose argument is display text and no others: new `ReplCommand::keeps_argument_whitespace` (the sigil/word lookup factored into `spec_for`, shared with `parse`). `edge_a_repeated_prompt_keeps_the_space_that_is_part_of_it` pins both sides — `>>> `/`rb> `/`rb> `, and `set x to 1   ` still recorded trimmed.

**3. MAJOR — no `:prompt` parse rows** (`commands.rs`)
Added bare / whitespace-only / trailing-space rows to `parse_reads_the_whole_alias_table` plus a `Prompt(Some(..))` arm, and `parse_reads_a_prompt_as_display_text_or_as_no_argument` asserting the three shapes whole, both sigils, and that other commands still trim.

**4. MAJOR — unbounded prompt format** (`mod.rs`)
`MAX_PROMPT_BYTES` (1024) enforced in `check_prompt_format`; the refusal quotes the size, not the format. `edge_an_oversize_prompt_format_is_refused_and_the_prompt_is_kept` asserts both sides of the boundary.

Each fix was mutation-checked (reverting it turns the new test red). Gates: fmt clean, clippy `-D warnings` clean, `cargo test` 1657 passed / 0 failed / 0 ignored across 63 binaries, all 7 examples exit 0. `phases/phase-055/REPORT.md` and `FINDINGS.md` updated with a round-1 section.
